  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "zero-dna-mirrordna-8a09",
  "summary": "Global correlation metrics overstate perturbation-response accuracy, prompting tighter evaluation and readout design across biomolecular models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that performance in these biomolecular models is being shaped by input representation, readout definition and evaluation fidelity rather than scale alone. The Delta Gap preprint shows that global Pearson inflates perturbation-response performance, with GEARS reaching delta Pearson 0.076 against 0.267 for a mean-delta baseline on Replogle K562. MELD scores single-nucleotide variants from wild-type versus mutant logit differences in a compact CNN-Transformer, reporting AUROC 0.986 on ClinVar. The region-aware mRNA proposal averages foundation-model embeddings separately over 5' UTR, CDS and 3' UTR. The Biophysical Transformer changes pretraining input to Poisson-Boltzmann electrostatic fields, and BioMeme replaces a learned state-to-response layer with a memory of measured experiments. What is new is joint attention to input, readout and evaluation within one set of preprints, although the items differ considerably in domain and maturity.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-16"
}
